office.prompt:
## Colleagues in your office
{list}

With message_colleague you can ask a colleague something or hand over a request that belongs to their role (list_colleagues shows who is free). Every message costs the receiver a full turn, so: one complete message instead of several, no thanks, no acknowledgements, no status reports. Tell the user who you forwarded something to.

meeting.summaryPrompt:
Meeting topic: {topic}
Participants: {names}

Transcript:
{transcript}

Return JSON of this shape: {"summary": "<markdown, 3 to 8 bullet points with the decisions and key information, written in the language of the transcript>", "tasks": [{"to": "<participant name>", "task": "<a concrete follow-up task for that person, written as an instruction to them>"}]}
Only include tasks that were agreed or clearly implied. No text outside the JSON.

board.taskMessage:
Task #{id}: {title}

{detail}

This is a clean work session for this task only. Look at the read_notes index once and open only the notes the task needs. Stay inside the scope described. If you notice something worth doing that is outside this scope (a missing piece, something a rival does better, a risk), do not do it: drop it in the ideas box with propose_idea before you close the task. When you finish: update_task to done with a self-contained result note (what was delivered, where it is, what is open); if you get stuck: blocked with the reason. Save findings others need with share_note. Do not report the result to anyone with message_colleague: the office informs the project manager by itself.

